#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054346 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/id #uuid "cff493c6-48c0-502b-9306-9f7bc262099d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13148" :question/problem "If $A = \\{1, 1, 2,1, 3,3\\}$, then what is $\\left|A\\right|?$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n1,\\qquad 2, \\qquad 3\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $A$ has $3$ elements, its cardinality is $|A| = 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054347 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Set With Set Elements"}] :question/id #uuid "3dd5ad9c-c449-5072-aebb-d8980dcc0ef1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13149" :question/problem "What is the cardinal number of $X = \\{ a, \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}, \\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\}, b \\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X{:}$\n\n$$\na, \\qquad \\emptyset, \\qquad \\{\\emptyset\\}, \\qquad \\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\}, \\qquad b\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- Only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\n- $\\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}$ and $\\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\}$ each count as single, distinct elements of $X.$\n\nSince $X$ has $5$ elements, the cardinality is $|X| = 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/id #uuid "e794793e-f22b-5072-be07-8b77d29d3b22" :question/math-academy-id "e-13169" :question/problem "If $A = \\{10, 19, 28,\\ldots,865\\},$ then what is $|A|?$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n10, \\quad 19, \\quad 28,\\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=9{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =9 \\\\  & =19-10 \\\\  & =28-19 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted $a_n,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =10+(n-1)\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =10+9n-9 \\\\  & =9n+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={9n+1:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in \\mathbb N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9N+1 & =865 \\\\ 9N & =864 \\\\ N & =\\frac{864}{9} \\\\ N & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{9n+1: n\\in \\mathbb N,\\: 1\\leq n \\leq 96  \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $96$ elements, we must have $|A| = 96.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054353 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/id #uuid "1acb903b-bdf0-5d16-8a1c-6fdce21f4c84" :question/math-academy-id "e-13172" :question/problem "If $A = \\{3, 21, 147,1\\,029,\\ldots,5\\,931\\,980\\,229\\},$ then what is $|A|?$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n3, \\quad 21, \\quad 147, \\quad 1\\,029,\\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=7{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =7 \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{147}{21} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted $a_n,$ is given by\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 r^{n-1} = 3(7^{n-1}) = \\dfrac37(7)^n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{\\dfrac37(7)^n : n\\in \\mathbb N,\\: 1\\leq n \\leq N \\right\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in \\mathbb N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}(7)^{N} & =5\\,931\\,980\\,229 \\\\ {7}^{N} & =13\\,841\\,287\\,201 \\\\ N & ={log}_{7}⁡(13\\,841\\,287\\,201) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(13\\,841\\,287\\,201)}{{log}_{10}⁡(7)} \\\\ N & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{\\dfrac37(7)^n : n\\in \\mathbb N,\\: 1\\leq n \\leq 12\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $12$ elements, we must have $|A| = 12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be82b906-a4c9-5b1b-8689-7a5cbb1fdba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306080} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d4debe-ac73-51da-88a0-74386019316c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306081} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c1bf35-8d6f-5145-a158-81ab011f84fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306082} {:answer/id #uuid "e584a6fd-fbe8-5436-85a3-3601c93905bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is infinite" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306083} {:answer/id #uuid "de60154c-9a97-5d4a-b322-863db049434b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c1bf35-8d6f-5145-a158-81ab011f84fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306082} :answer-field/id #uuid "0992e4e0-ead1-5f3b-83a0-0fb13687bd5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9ec915a-acd9-5cc8-a3ce-0880d90635bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-104887" :question/problem "If $X={{3}^{2},{5}^{2},{7}^{2},{9}^{2}}$, then $|X|=$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\n{3}^{2},\\,{5}^{2},\\,{7}^{2},\\,{9}^{2}\n$$\n\nSince $X$ has $4$ elements, its cardinality is $|X|=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "f2801469-fcbb-52a5-b26b-9773c73cabba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051845}] :question/id #uuid "d64c45b7-2d40-58ad-9748-05e941de30d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-181454" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nIf $A = {3, 6, 12, 24, 48, …, 98304}$, then $\\mid A|=$ {{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5ac7f2-4727-542b-97f5-91ade2a1301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d5ac7f2-4727-542b-97f5-91ade2a1301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306089} :answer-field/id #uuid "146a0fb6-b5f9-578e-a298-762346302c0f" :answer-f