722445be-c593-5089-a589-eccdb901213a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80737" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $A={∅,{∅},{{∅}}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n∅,\\,{∅},\\,{{∅}}\n$$\n\nNote that $∅,$ ${∅},$ and ${{∅}}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=3.$"}]}
